From 9e7675d428af0d74c2883bf728b60405fa088146 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:26:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] MEM2 step 2: unlock_by_id's id map is generated const
 data (GBA EWRAM +2,048 B)

unlocks.c built ul_by_id[1024] (int16, 2,048 B of .bss) from the registry at first use.
ulgen now writes it next to X3's key index (core/gen/unlock_index.c doomo_ul_by_id, ROM on
the GBA); ul_by_check() proves it is the registry's first-entry-per-id map and finds
duplicate ids as before, and a stale file falls back to a registry scan (slow, not wrong).
The PS1 has no index (its EXE is RAM) and keeps the table as it was: no PS1 byte changes.
GBA: EWRAM free 50,740 -> 52,788 B; IWRAM unchanged.

Test: mem2_unlock_by_id_map_matches_the_scan (every id, map against scan, and the owned
count); unlock_index_active() now also needs the id map, so a stale file fails x3's check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
